1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:06,875
An entity-relationship diagram is a map of tables before they become SQL, or beside the SQL.

2
00:00:06,875 --> 00:00:08,611
A box is an entity.

3
00:00:08,611 --> 00:00:11,555
The name on the box is the table you expect.

4
00:00:11,555 --> 00:00:14,180
Inside the box you list attributes.

5
00:00:14,180 --> 00:00:15,972
You mark the primary key.

6
00:00:15,972 --> 00:00:20,236
You mark foreign keys as copies of someone else's primary key.

7
00:00:20,236 --> 00:00:22,375
A line is a relationship.

8
00:00:22,375 --> 00:00:26,722
The ends of the line carry cardinality: one or many.

9
00:00:26,722 --> 00:00:28,569
A crow's foot means many.

10
00:00:28,569 --> 00:00:30,375
A single bar means one.

11
00:00:30,375 --> 00:00:32,875
A circle means zero is allowed.

12
00:00:32,875 --> 00:00:35,444
A second bar means one is required.

13
00:00:35,444 --> 00:00:38,347
You do not need every symbol on day one.

14
00:00:38,347 --> 00:00:41,902
You need boxes, keys, and honest lines.

15
00:00:41,902 --> 00:00:43,916
Read a line as a sentence.

16
00:00:43,916 --> 00:00:46,319
One customer places many orders.

17
00:00:46,319 --> 00:00:48,875
Each order belongs to one customer.

18
00:00:48,875 --> 00:00:52,638
If you cannot say the sentence, the line is decoration.

19
00:00:52,638 --> 00:00:55,847
Do not draw a line labeled after a one-off demo.

20
00:00:55,847 --> 00:00:58,027
Draw the store you are actually building.

21
00:00:58,027 --> 00:01:02,805
Keep example names ordinary: customers, orders, books.

22
00:01:02,805 --> 00:01:07,555
A diagram that uses joke names will be quoted as if they were tables.

23
00:01:07,555 --> 00:01:11,458
Attributes that are only display labels stay off the line.

24
00:01:11,458 --> 00:01:13,666
The line is not where you write total.

25
00:01:13,666 --> 00:01:15,486
total lives in a box.

26
00:01:15,486 --> 00:01:19,597
When a relationship has its own attributes, it wants a box.

27
00:01:19,597 --> 00:01:21,277
Enrollment has a grade.

28
00:01:21,277 --> 00:01:23,500
That is the many-to-many lesson.

29
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,291
On the diagram, the middle box is a real entity.

30
00:01:27,291 --> 00:01:28,986
Layout is pedagogy.

31
00:01:28,986 --> 00:01:30,930
Put the hub table in the middle.

32
00:01:30,930 --> 00:01:34,236
customers in the center, orders to the side.

33
00:01:34,236 --> 00:01:36,597
Do not cross lines if you can avoid it.

34
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:39,277
The drawing should match the join you will write.

35
00:01:39,277 --> 00:01:41,847
Update the diagram when you ALTER.

36
00:01:41,847 --> 00:01:44,111
A stale picture is worse than none.

37
00:01:44,111 --> 00:01:47,194
The point is not software that draws cylinders.

38
00:01:47,194 --> 00:01:54,319
The point is a shared sentence: these are the things, these are the keys, these are the allowed counts.

39
00:01:54,319 --> 00:01:57,083
Crow's foot is not the only notation.

40
00:01:57,083 --> 00:02:00,486
Chen diagrams use diamonds for relationships.

41
00:02:00,486 --> 00:02:06,152
IDEF1X uses dots and crow's feet with different mandatory marks.

42
00:02:06,152 --> 00:02:08,250
Pick one notation for a team.

43
00:02:08,250 --> 00:02:12,861
Mixing them is how a bar gets read as optional when it meant mandatory.

44
00:02:12,861 --> 00:02:18,416
Subtype boxes appear when a customer is either a person or an organization.

45
00:02:18,416 --> 00:02:20,583
That is a later modeling choice.

46
00:02:20,583 --> 00:02:24,472
Do not draw it on day one unless the facts already split.

47
00:02:24,472 --> 00:02:26,208
Color is not notation.

48
00:02:26,208 --> 00:02:30,819
A calm diagram in one ink beats a rainbow of departments.

49
00:02:30,819 --> 00:02:34,319
Your player uses a dark calm stage for the same reason.

50
00:02:34,319 --> 00:02:38,805
Print the diagram at the size a new engineer can read on one screen.

51
00:02:38,805 --> 00:02:42,722
If you need a poster, you have too many boxes for one talk.

52
00:02:42,722 --> 00:02:47,722
Split by bounded context: catalog, checkout, fulfillment.

53
00:02:47,722 --> 00:02:51,541
Each picture should still use the same names for the shared keys.

54
00:02:51,541 --> 00:02:55,819
customer_id is customer_id everywhere.

55
00:02:55,819 --> 00:02:59,652
A glossary next to the pictures beats clever synonyms.

56
00:02:59,652 --> 00:03:04,819
When a line has numbers, 1 and 0..* are enough.

57
00:03:04,819 --> 00:03:07,069
Do not write a paragraph on the line.

58
00:03:07,069 --> 00:03:10,375
Put the paragraph in a comment on the foreign key.

59
00:03:10,375 --> 00:03:12,263
The diagram is the map.

60
00:03:12,263 --> 00:03:14,277
The SQL is the territory.

61
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:17,625
Walk both, in that order, until they agree.

62
00:03:17,625 --> 00:03:20,666
Then the next join is a line you already drew.

63
00:03:20,666 --> 00:03:24,736
A diagram that cannot be read in two minutes is a mural.

64
00:03:24,736 --> 00:03:26,347
Murals do not ship.

65
00:03:26,347 --> 00:03:30,111
Cut until a new person can say the sentences on the lines.

66
00:03:30,111 --> 00:03:35,083
If they invent a table that is not on the page, the page is incomplete.

67
00:03:35,083 --> 00:03:39,527
If they cannot find a table that is in SQL, the page is stale.

68
00:03:39,527 --> 00:03:44,541
Incomplete and stale are the only two diagram failures that matter.

69
00:03:44,541 --> 00:03:45,916
Pretty is optional.

70
00:03:45,916 --> 00:03:47,319
Agreement is not.

71
00:03:47,319 --> 00:03:48,569
Print the keys.

72
00:03:48,569 --> 00:03:49,875
Print the counts.

73
00:03:49,875 --> 00:03:51,666
Sit the SQL beside it.

74
00:03:51,666 --> 00:03:53,916
When they match, you have a map.

75
00:03:53,916 --> 00:04:02,861
An entity-relationship diagram is a picture of what you will store and how those things connect, drawn before CREATE TABLE hardens a guess.

76
00:04:02,861 --> 00:04:06,763
Entities are the things: customer, product, order.

77
00:04:06,763 --> 00:04:08,680
They appear as rectangles.

78
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:15,861
Attributes are the facts inside the rectangle: name, email, price, with types once you know them.

79
00:04:15,861 --> 00:04:23,263
Relationships are how entities participate: a customer places an order, an order contains products.

80
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:31,944
Chen notation uses diamonds for relationships, and it showed up in a 1976 paper, which is why textbooks still teach it.

81
00:04:31,944 --> 00:04:41,166
Crow's foot notation uses lines and little marks at the ends for cardinality, and practitioners sketch it on whiteboards because it is fast.

82
00:04:41,166 --> 00:04:42,625
Neither is more true.

83
00:04:42,625 --> 00:04:45,500
Switching mid-diagram is what is false.

84
00:04:45,626 --> 00:04:54,645
A complete diagram names the entities, the attributes you will actually store, the relationships, and the cardinalities once you know them.

85
00:04:54,645 --> 00:04:57,978
It is a map, not a screenshot of the application.

86
00:04:57,978 --> 00:04:59,603
Screens have buttons.

87
00:04:59,603 --> 00:05:02,506
Diagrams have identity and connection.

88
00:05:02,506 --> 00:05:05,589
Start by placing the entities you already found.

89
00:05:05,589 --> 00:05:11,423
Then ask, for each pair that your interviews connected, whether a relationship belongs.

90
00:05:11,423 --> 00:05:13,353
Not every pair gets a line.

91
00:05:13,353 --> 00:05:17,784
Customers and manufacturers might only meet through products.

92
00:05:17,784 --> 00:05:19,298
Draw the real verb.

93
00:05:19,298 --> 00:05:23,228
places, contains, reviews, works for.

94
00:05:23,228 --> 00:05:27,117
If you cannot name the verb, you do not have a relationship yet.

95
00:05:27,117 --> 00:05:29,381
You have two boxes on a poster.

96
00:05:29,381 --> 00:05:32,520
Cardinality marks wait for the next lessons.

97
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:38,826
Here the skill is connecting without spaghetti: every line is a sentence from requirements.

98
00:05:38,826 --> 00:05:41,034
The benefit is forgetting less.

99
00:05:41,034 --> 00:05:45,492
A missing line is a join you will fake with a comment in six months.

100
00:05:45,492 --> 00:05:49,076
An extra line is a constraint you cannot explain.

101
00:05:49,076 --> 00:05:52,117
Read the diagram out loud as sentences.

102
00:05:52,117 --> 00:05:56,020
If a sentence was never said in gathering, erase the line.

103
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:59,742
If a sentence was said and there is no line, draw it.

104
00:05:59,742 --> 00:06:04,923
Then you are ready to talk about one, many, and identifying relationships.

